 Georgetown student tradition for years and documents visits to three embassies.","source_url":"https://www.georgetown.edu/news/the-best-halloween-traditions-at-georgetown/","source_title":"The Best Halloween Traditions at Georgetown","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2023-11-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Participation is embassy-specific and not guaranteed; verify current public access, security requirements and hours directly.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gu-hoya-saxa-chant","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Hoya Saxa Chant","title":"Answer the Crowd with Hoya Saxa","subtitle":"Georgetown’s century-old Greek-and-Latin cheer","notes":"Listen for the pep band’s cue at an official game, follow the student section’s cadence and treat the debated origin as unresolved history.","short_summary":"A hybrid-language yell first printed in the 1890s still supplies Georgetown’s defining game-day response.","evidence_claim":"Georgetown reported in 2025 that “Hoya Saxa” means “what rocks” and has served as the university’s cheer for more than 100 years.","source_url":"https://www.georgetown.edu/news/what-being-a-hoya-means-to-the-2025-2026-georgetown-storytellers/","source_title":"What Being a Hoya Means to the 2025-2026 Georgetown Storytellers","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-10-10","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Most readily heard at official athletics events; event admission and venue rules vary by game.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
